# =====================================================================
# JCER E-CELL — Migration 001 API-level staging tests (PostgREST)
# STATUS: NOT RUN. Requires a STAGING Supabase project with Migration 001
#   applied and real Auth users. Run with the VS Code "REST Client"
#   extension (no install) or translate each block to curl.
#
# Fill the variables below from the staging project:
#   @baseUrl   = https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
#   @anonKey   = the project ANON (public) key  (NEVER the service-role key)
#   @aJwt/@bJwt/@adminJwt = access_token from a real sign-in of each user
#   (Sign in via the Auth REST endpoint or the dashboard; copy access_token.)
#   Replace <STUDENT_A_UUID>/<STUDENT_B_UUID> with the real auth UUIDs.
#
# PostgREST maps: GET /rest/v1/<table>, RPC via POST /rest/v1/rpc/<fn>.
# =====================================================================

@baseUrl = https://REPLACE.supabase.co
@anonKey = REPLACE_ANON_KEY
@aJwt = REPLACE_STUDENT_A_ACCESS_TOKEN
@bJwt = REPLACE_STUDENT_B_ACCESS_TOKEN
@adminJwt = REPLACE_ADMIN_ACCESS_TOKEN
@contentType = application/json

### A1. anon reads the public view -> 200, only the 11 public columns.
###     Expect: 200; objects have slug/full_name/... and NO id/email/usn.
GET {{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/public_profiles?select=*&limit=1
apikey: {{anonKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{anonKey}}

### A2. anon requests a private column through the view.
###     Expect: 400 (column does not exist in the view).
GET {{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/public_profiles?select=email
apikey: {{anonKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{anonKey}}

### A3. anon reads the base profiles table.
###     Expect: 200 with [] (RLS exposes no rows to anon) — never private data.
GET {{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/profiles?select=*
apikey: {{anonKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{anonKey}}

### A4. anon writes the base table. Expect: 401/403 (no grant / RLS).
POST {{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/profiles
apikey: {{anonKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{anonKey}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "full_name": "x" }

### A5. Student A reads own profile -> 200 with exactly one row.
GET {{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/profiles?select=*&id=eq.<STUDENT_A_UUID>
apikey: {{anonKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{aJwt}}

### A6. Student A reads Student B's profile -> 200 with [] (RLS isolation).
GET {{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/profiles?select=*&id=eq.<STUDENT_B_UUID>
apikey: {{anonKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{aJwt}}

### A7. Student A directly PATCHes a protected column (status).
###     Expect: 403 (column not granted). Proves clients cannot self-approve.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/profiles?id=eq.<STUDENT_A_UUID>
apikey: {{anonKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{aJwt}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Prefer: return=representation

{ "status": "approved" }

### A8. Student A PATCHes an allowed content column -> 200 (one row).
###     (On an approved profile this also forces pending_review via trigger.)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/profiles?id=eq.<STUDENT_A_UUID>
apikey: {{anonKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{aJwt}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Prefer: return=representation

{ "bio": "updated via API" }

### A9. Student A submits own profile via RPC -> 200.
POST {{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/rpc/submit_my_profile
apikey: {{anonKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{aJwt}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{}

### A10. Student A calls admin_review_profile -> 403 (not admin).
POST {{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/rpc/admin_review_profile
apikey: {{anonKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{aJwt}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "p_profile_id": "<STUDENT_B_UUID>", "p_status": "approved", "p_reviewed_updated_at": "2000-01-01T00:00:00Z" }

### -------------------------------------------------------------------
### SEQUENCING for A11-A15 — run in order; the profile's status evolves:
###   A11 requires <STUDENT_A_UUID> to be 'pending_review'. If it is not,
###       first submit it: POST /rest/v1/rpc/submit_my_profile (as Student A).
###   A12 rejects it -> status becomes 'rejected'.
###   Before A15, RESUBMIT to 'pending_review' (POST /rest/v1/rpc/submit_my_profile
###       as Student A) so A15 exercises the concurrency check, not the
###       not-pending rejection.
###   Before A14, the profile must be 'approved' (approve via A11 again).
###   Reset the profile's status between groups as needed; do not assume the
###       order alone leaves it in the required state.
### -------------------------------------------------------------------
### A11. Admin approves a pending profile via RPC -> 200 (approved row).
###      First GET the profile's current updated_at (as admin) and paste it into
###      p_reviewed_updated_at VERBATIM (do not reformat through Date):
###        GET {{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/profiles?select=updated_at&id=eq.<STUDENT_A_UUID>
POST {{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/rpc/admin_review_profile
apikey: {{anonKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminJwt}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "p_profile_id": "<STUDENT_A_UUID>", "p_status": "approved", "p_reviewed_updated_at": "<STUDENT_A_UPDATED_AT>", "p_is_featured": true }

### A12. Admin rejects with a reason -> 200 (rejected row).
POST {{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/rpc/admin_review_profile
apikey: {{anonKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminJwt}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "p_profile_id": "<STUDENT_A_UUID>", "p_status": "rejected", "p_reviewed_updated_at": "<STUDENT_A_UPDATED_AT>", "p_rejection_reason": "insufficient proof" }

### A13. Admin RPC with null status -> 400 with SQLSTATE 22023 in the body.
POST {{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/rpc/admin_review_profile
apikey: {{anonKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminJwt}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "p_profile_id": "<STUDENT_A_UUID>", "p_status": null, "p_reviewed_updated_at": "2000-01-01T00:00:00Z" }

### A15. Admin reviews with a STALE updated_at -> 400 P0001 "changed"; the
###      profile stays pending. PRECONDITION: the profile MUST be 'pending_review'
###      (resubmit it first via submit_my_profile). Use a GENUINELY stale
###      p_reviewed_updated_at (e.g. an old timestamp like the one below), NOT the
###      profile's current updated_at, so this exercises the optimistic-concurrency
###      check rather than the "not pending review" rejection.
POST {{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/rpc/admin_review_profile
apikey: {{anonKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminJwt}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "p_profile_id": "<STUDENT_A_UUID>", "p_status": "approved", "p_reviewed_updated_at": "2000-01-01T00:00:00Z" }

### A14. Student withdraws approved profile via RPC -> 200 (draft row),
###      then confirm it disappears from public_profiles (re-run A1).
POST {{baseUrl}}/rest/v1/rpc/withdraw_my_profile
apikey: {{anonKey}}
Authorization: Bearer {{aJwt}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{}

